<br>

Our group develops physics-based models and advanced manufacturing strategies to understand and control the thermal, mechanical, and materials-level phenomena governing solid-state and additive manufacturing processes. By uncovering fundamental process–structure–property relationships, we enable predictive simulation, process optimization, defect mitigation, and microstructure control. These capabilities advance the reliability, performance, and scalability of next-generation solid-state and additive manufacturing technologies.<br>
<br>
<b> Our current research directions:</b>
<ul>
<li> <b> Physics-based and multiphysics modeling of additive and solid-state manufacturing processe</b> </li>
<li> <b> Process–structure–property relationships and microstructure evolution </b> </li>
<li> <b> Predictive modeling and simulation-driven process optimization</b> </li>
<li> <b> Defect formation, mitigation, and process–material interactions
<br>
</ul>

